c Reasons: None\n    - Pros: No statement in the predicted reasons directly addresses mucinous cystadenoma or its consistency with imaging findings.\n    - Cons: None.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 5: Serous cystadenoma was suggested intraoperatively, but the presence of a significant fibrous stromal component on final histology reclassified the lesion — “Intraoperative histopathology revealed a serous cystadenoma... the final histopathologic examination revealed ovarian cystadenofibroma.”\n- Potential match from Predicted Diagnostic Reasons: None\n    - Pros: No statement in the predicted reasons discusses the intraoperative findings, final histology, or reclassification of the lesion.\n    - Cons: None.\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\n- Groundtruth 1: No match.\n- Groundtruth 2: Matches Predicted 2 because both discuss dysgerminoma being less likely due to tumor markers.\n- Groundtruth 3: No match.\n- Groundtruth 4: No match.\n- Groundtruth 5: No match.\n\n</diagnostic_comparison>\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [\n      \"The patient has a large ovarian tumor, elevated LDH, and abdominal distension, which could be indicative of a dysgerminoma, although the absence of solid components on CT and the specific tumor markers make it less likely than serous ovarian tumor.\"\n    ],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": [],\n    \"5\": []\n  }\n}\n```",
