  "085a149285b72d239caf70c926849c30157555ce7951fe2b79fdf20b788a924e": {
    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. A Bartholin gland cyst was initially considered but excluded because of the patient’s age and absence of pain or discomfort with activity — “The cyst was excluded, because it is more common in young women, and causes symptoms of pain during walking, sitting, and intercourse, which were absent in this case.”\n2. Chondroid syringoma was diagnosed three times due to the lesion’s slow growth, encapsulation, and painless, solid features — “CS — which is also known as pleomorphic adenoma or benign mixed tumor — is a rare encapsulated, slow-growing, well-defined, painless and solid tumor.”\n3. Clear cell hidradenoma was considered after the second excision because of the lobular architecture of cuboidal cells without atypia — “lobular glandular proliferation of cuboid cells with no anaplasia.”\n4. Adenoid cystic carcinoma became the leading diagnosis when histology showed a characteristic cribriform architecture with nests of basaloid cells amid hyalinized stroma — “The cribriform pattern is the most typical characterization, which is formed by nests of tumor cells interrupted by basophilic basement membrane materials.”\n\nPredicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. The patient's history of a slowly enlarging mass in the left labia majora, firm and painless, with multiple recurrences and histopathology showing chondroid syringoma, supports this diagnosis. The mass's characteristics, such as being well-circumscribed and having normal vital signs and laboratory tests, are also consistent with chondroid syringoma.\n2. The patient's history of a slowly enlarging mass in the left labia majora, firm and painless, with multiple recurrences and histopathology consistently showing chondroid syringoma, supports this diagnosis.\n3. The patient's history of a recurrence in the labia majora with histology showing clear cell hidradenoma, characterized by lobular glandular proliferation of cuboid cells with no anaplasia, supports this diagnosis.\n\nAnalysis of potential matches:\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 1: A Bartholin gland cyst was initially considered but excluded because of the patient’s age and absence of pain or discomfort with activity — “The cyst was excluded, because it is more common in young women, and causes symptoms of pain during walking, sitting, and intercourse, which were absent in this case.”\n- No direct match in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. The predicted reasons focus on supporting the diagnoses of Chondroid Syringoma and Clear Cell Hidradenoma, not on excluding other conditions.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 2: Chondroid syringoma was diagnosed three times due to the lesion’s slow growth, encapsulation, and painless, solid features — “CS — which is also known as pleomorphic adenoma or benign mixed tumor — is a rare encapsulated, slow-growing, well-defined, painless and solid tumor.”\n- Potential match 1: \"The patient's history of a slowly enlarging mass in the left labia majora, firm and painless, with multiple recurrences and histopathology showing chondroid syringoma, supports this diagnosis. The mass's characteristics, such as being well-circumscribed and having normal vital signs and laboratory tests, are also consistent with chondroid syringoma.\"\n    - Pros: Mentions \"slowly enlarging mass,\" \"firm and painless,\" which directly align with \"slow growth\" and \"painless, solid features\" from the ground truth. It also explicitly states \"histopathology showing chondroid syringoma,\" linking these features to the diagnosis. The \"well-circumscribed\" characteristic is similar to \"encapsulated\" or \"well-defined.\"\n    - Cons: Does not explicitly use the word \"encapsulation\" or \"solid features\" verbatim, but \"firm\" and \"well-circumscribed\" convey similar meanings.\n- Potential match 2: \"The patient's history of a slowly enlarging mass in the left labia majora, firm and painless, with multiple recurrences and histopathology consistently showing chondroid syringoma, supports this diagnosis.\"\n    - Pros: Mentions \"slowly enlarging mass,\" \"firm and painless,\" and \"histopathology consistently showing chondroid syringoma,\" which are strong matches for the ground truth's description of chondroid syringoma's features and its diagnosis.\n    - Cons: Less comprehensive than Predicted Reason 1 as it omits \"well-circumscribed.\"\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 3: Clear cell hidradenoma was considered after the second excision because of the lobular architecture of cuboidal cells without atypia — “lobular glandular proliferation of cuboid cells with no anaplasia.”\n- Potential match 1: \"The patient's history of a recurrence in the labia majora with histology showing clear cell hidradenoma, characterized by lobular glandular proliferation of cuboid cells with no anaplasia, supports this diagnosis.\"\n    - Pros: Directly quotes \"lobular glandular proliferation of cuboid cells with no anaplasia,\" which is the exact histological description provided in the ground truth for clear cell hidradenoma. It also links this to the diagnosis of clear cell hidradenoma.\n    - Cons: None, this is a very strong and direct match.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 4: Adenoid cystic carcinoma became the leading diagnosis when histology showed a characteristic cribriform architecture with nests of basaloid cells amid hyalinized stroma — “The cribriform pattern is the most typical characterization, which is formed by nests of tumor cells interrupted by basophilic basement membrane materials.”\n- No direct match in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. The predicted reasons do not discuss adenoid cystic carcinoma.\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\n- For Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 1, there are no matches in the Predicted Diagnostic Reasons.\n- For Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 2, Predicted Diagnostic Reason 1 and Predicted Diagnostic Reason 2 both provide strong support, mentioning \"slowly enlarging mass,\" \"firm and painless,\" and linking these to the diagnosis of chondroid syringoma. Predicted Reason 1 also adds \"well-circumscribed\" which aligns with \"encapsulated.\"\n- For Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 3, Predicted Diagnostic Reason 3 is a direct and verbatim match for the histological description.\n- For Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 4, there are no matches in the Predicted Diagnostic Reasons.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [\n      \"The patient's history of a slowly enlarging mass in the left labia majora, firm and painless, with multiple recurrences and histopathology showing chondroid syringoma, supports this diagnosis. The mass's characteristics, such as being well-circumscribed and having normal vital signs and laboratory tests, are also consistent with chondroid syringoma.\",\n      \"The patient's history of a slowly enlarging mass in the left labia majora, firm and painless, with multiple recurrences and histopathology consistently showing chondroid syringoma, supports this diagnosis.\"\n    ],\n    \"3\": [\n      \"The patient's history of a recurrence in the labia majora with histology showing clear cell hidradenoma, characterized by lobular glandular proliferation of cuboid cells with no anaplasia, supports this diagnosis.\"\n    ],\n    \"4\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n</diagnostic_comparison>",
    "prompt_id": "mcr.reasoning_recall"
