  "48997b8f8345f870a24ad0972b92da74b051cd8284b38489a5cd1a08600b235f": {
    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. Gastric outlet obstruction was considered given the patient’s intractable vomiting and abdominal distension — “…differential diagnoses were considered given the above presentation: • Gastric outlet obstruction.”\n2. Peptic stricture of the stomach was considered as a cause of outlet narrowing — “…differential diagnoses were considered given the above presentation: • Peptic stricture of the stomach.”\n3. Neoplasm of the stomach was considered because tumors can obstruct gastric outflow — “…differential diagnoses were considered given the above presentation: • Neoplasm of the stomach.”\n4. Annular pancreas, diabetic gastroparesis, internal hernia, and duodenal bezoar were considered as alternative causes of obstruction but were excluded by endoscopy — “An upper gastrointestinal endoscopy was also done to rule out other causes and it was found to be normal.”\n5. Peptic ulcer disease and duodenal tumors were also considered among other causes of obstruction and were excluded by imaging and endoscopy — “…other causes of duodenal obstruction like peptic ulcer disease and duodenal tumors.”\n6. Scleroderma and other collagen or vascular disorders were considered as mimics of the presentation — “…conditions that closely mimic SMA syndrome ranging from scleroderma to other collagen and vascular disorders…”\n7. Vascular compression due to a reduced aortomesenteric angle was supported by CT findings demonstrating duodenal compression — “CT scans were used to rule in for duodenal obstruction due to a reduced aortomesenteric angle in the patient.”\n\nPredicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. The patient has intractable vomiting, postprandial upper abdominal pain, and marked gastric distension. The compression of the third portion of the duodenum between the superior mesenteric artery and the aorta at an acute angle is a key finding that supports this diagnosis.\n2. The patient presents with intractable vomiting, po