oma) … The histopathology was negative for EBV, positive for lymphoma markers CD-10, B-cell lymphoma 6 protein (BCL-6) and multiple myeloma oncogene 1 (MUM1); and positive for CD-20.”\"\n- Potential matches from Predicted Diagnostic Reasons: None.\n    - Pros: No statements in the predicted reasons discuss non-epithelial tumors, lymphoma, sarcoma, or immunophenotyping markers like CD-20 or CD-10. The predicted reasons focus on infectious processes.\n    - Cons: None.\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\nThere are no matching statements between the Groundtruth Diagnostic Reasons and the Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. The groundtruth reasons discuss the differential diagnosis and exclusion of various types of bladder malignancies based on biopsy and immunophenotyping, ultimately confirming lymphoma. The predicted reasons, however, focus entirely on diagnosing urinary tract infection and pyelonephritis based on symptoms, lab results, and imaging findings related to infection. The two sets of reasons are discussing completely different diagnostic pathways and conditions.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n</diagnostic_comparison>",
