r cancer\" based on symptoms and imaging.\n- Pros: None.\n- Cons: No mention of seminoma or its likelihood.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 2: Germ cell tumor (gonadoblastoma) was considered but germ cell markers were absent — “Immunohistochemical results are often positive for PLAP, OCT3/4, and SALL-4.”\n- This statement discusses a specific differential diagnosis (germ cell tumor/gonadoblastoma) and the absence of specific germ cell markers. It also mentions what markers are typically positive.\n- Predicted Diagnostic Reasons do not mention germ cell tumors, gonadoblastoma, or specific germ cell markers like PLAP, OCT3/4, or SALL-4. One predicted reason mentions \"tumor markers are not typical for this diagnosis\" but doesn't specify which markers or which diagnosis it refers to in the context of germ cell tumors.\n- Pros: None.\n- Cons: No mention of germ cell tumor, gonadoblastoma, or specific germ cell markers.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 3: Endometrioid carcinoma with cord-like differentiation was considered but the typical immunoprofile did not match (CK7+, EMA+, inhibin-α–, WT1–) — “The cytokeratin 7 (CK7), epithelial membrane antigen (EMA) positive and inhibin-α, calretinin, WT1 negative immunostaining pattern is more supported an endometrioid carcinoma.”\n- This statement discusses a specific differential diagnosis (endometrioid carcinoma) and its typical immunoprofile, noting that the patient's profile did not match.\n- Predicted Diagnostic Reasons do not mention endometrioid carcinoma or any specific immunoprofile markers like CK7, EMA, inhibin-α, or WT1.\n- Pros: None.\n- Cons: No mention of endometrioid carcinoma or specific immunoprofile markers.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 4: Mixed Sertoli–Leydig cell tumor was considered but characteristic Leydig cell features were absent — “Reinke crystals in the cytoplasm can be clearly confirmed.”\n- This statement discusses a specific differential diagnosis (Mixed Sertoli–Leydig cell tumor) and the absence of characteristic Leydig cell features (Reinke crystals).\n- Predicted Diagnostic Reasons do not mention Sertoli–Leydig cell tumor or Reinke crystals.\n- Pros: None.\n- Cons: No mention of Sertoli–Leydig cell tumor or Reinke crystals.\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\nThere are no direct matches between the Groundtruth Diagnostic Reasons and the Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. The Groundtruth reasons delve into specific differential diagnoses and their supporting/contradicting immunohistochemical or pathological features, while the Predicted reasons provide general evidence for a \"testicular tumor\" or \"testicular cancer\" based on clinical presentation and imaging.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n</diagnostic_comparison>",
