redicted reasons focus on DILI and cholestatic jaundice, not the exclusion of autoimmune hepatitis.\n- Groundtruth 3: No direct match. The predicted reasons focus on DILI and cholestatic jaundice, not the exclusion of metabolic liver diseases.\n- Groundtruth 4: Predicted reason C is a partial match. While it doesn't explicitly state the imaging findings, it discusses \"cholestatic jaundice\" and then argues for DILI as a more likely diagnosis, implying that other causes of cholestasis (including obstructive) were considered and found less likely.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": [\n      \"The patient has jaundice with elevated alkaline phosphatase and γ-glutamyl transferase, which are characteristic of cholestatic jaundice. However, the presence of elevated liver enzymes and bilirubin levels, as well as the temporal relationship with Alfuzosin use, makes drug-induced liver injury a more likely diagnosis.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n</diagnostic_comparison>",
