  "f000c68139d6703f189aeab19b5fc7db77ce4277a6997ca1fb35f80ecd622e98": {
    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. Phyllodes tumor was excluded by its characteristic pericanalicular fibroadenoma pattern and lack of atypia on histology — “glands were lined by bilayered epithelium with pericanalicular pattern of fibroadenoma and absence of cytological atypia.”\n2. Virginal hypertrophy was excluded by the finding of a discrete, well‐encapsulated tumor rather than diffuse glandular enlargement — “the specimen was sent for histopathological examination which showed well encapsulated tumor with hyperplasia of both epithelial and stromal components.”\n3. Adenocarcinoma was excluded by the absence of cytological atypia on histopathology — “absence of cytological atypia.”\n4. Tuberculosis was excluded by normal inflammatory markers and imaging — “Chest X-ray was normal.”\n\nPredicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n- \"The patient's presentation of a well-circumscribed, firm, non-tender, mobile lump, along with ultrasonography and fine-needle aspiration cytology results suggestive of fibroadenoma, strongly supports this diagnosis.\"\n- \"The patient presents with a well-circumscribed, firm, non-tender, mobile lump, and ultrasonography and fine-needle aspiration cytology results are consistent with fibroadenoma.\"\n\nFor each Groundtruth statement, consider potential matches:\n\nStatement 1: Phyllodes tumor excluded by pericanalicular pattern and lack of atypia. Predicted statements do not mention histology, pericanalicular pattern, bilayered epithelium, or cytological atypia. They only mention clinical and imaging findings. No match. Pros: none. Cons: completely different content.\n\nStatement 2: Virginal hypertrophy excluded by discrete, well-encapsulated tumor. Predicted statements mention \"well-circumscribed\" lump, which is similar to \"well-encapsulated tumor\", but the groundtruth explicitly contrasts with diffuse enlargement, and the predicted statements do not mention encapsulation or exclusion of diffuse enlargement. Also, the groundtruth refers to histopathological examination, while predicted refers to clinical and ultrasonography/fine-needle aspiration. The match is not exact; the phrase \"well-circumscribed\" is not the same as \"well-encapsulated\" and the context of exclusion is missing. So no match.\n\nStatement 3: Adenocarcinoma excluded by absence of cytological atypia. Predicted statements do not mention cytological atypia or absence of malignancy. No match.\n\nStatement 4: Tuberculosis excluded by normal chest X-ray and inflammatory markers. Predicted statements do not mention chest X-ray or inflammatory markers. No match.\n\nSummary: No Groundtruth diagnostic reason has a matching statement in the Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. All lists are empty.\n</diagnostic_comparison>\n\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": []\n  }\n}",
    "prompt_id": "mcr.reasoning_recall"
